  count and number of spectral variables on logarithmic axes; colours separate
  regression and classification rows, and the inset summarizes coarse
  application domains.}
  \label{fig:dataset_diversity}
\end{figure}

Table~\ref{tab:dataset_statistics} summarizes the cohort in the same compact
form used for the companion benchmark inventory.  Regression contains 61 rows
with median $n=402$ samples and median $p=1023$ spectral variables.
Classification contains 17 rows with median $n=511$ and median $p=1951$; the
median number of classes is two and the median largest-class share is 0.513.
The complete per-dataset description is provided in the supplementary
longtable.

